<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Andosini</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pyrenean people subdued by Hannibal on his march to Italy in 218 BCE, often linked with the name of Andorra.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Andosini are known only from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>, who lists them among the peoples between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> conquered in 218 BCE. They are usually placed in the high valleys around modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/andorra">Andorra</a>, whose name is often thought to derive from theirs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their society beyond a probable mountain economy of herding and small-scale farming.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal's</a> campaign their territory was left under the Carthaginian officer Hanno. Following the Roman victories in the north-east and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato</a>'s campaign of 195 BCE, the area passed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, and the Andosini are not mentioned again.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 300 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:2.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/andorra">Andorra</a>, <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Andosins</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-248&amp;focus=andosini" aria-label="Andosini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4717 665 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Andosini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4975 1081h0M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5037 921h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5037 921h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Andorra. <a href="/atlas?year=-248&amp;focus=andosini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
